  "id": "nicotine-withdrawal",
  "term": "nicotine withdrawal",
  "definition": "Nicotine withdrawal is a mental health condition that can happen after a person stops using nicotine. It commonly involves craving nicotine, irritability, anxiety, low mood, and increased appetite, and these symptoms can begin quickly and may lead the person to start using nicotine again.",
